    <dashboard name='Story Teller' type='storyboard'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff007f'>Story Teller</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='964' maxwidth='1016' minheight='964' minwidth='1016' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98340' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98426' x='787' y='830'>
            <zone h='4253' id='3' type-v2='title' w='98426' x='787' y='830' />
            <zone h='10477' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='98426' x='787' y='5083' />
            <zone h='83610' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98426' x='787' y='15560'>
              <flipboard active-id='7' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='Compare the number of fraudulent job postings across industries to identify sectors most frequently targeted by recruitment scams.' captured-sheet='Fraud Count by Industry' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='Analyze how fraudulent job postings are distributed across different employment types to identify high-risk recruitment categories.' captured-sheet='Fraud by Employment Type' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='Measure the percentage of fraudulent job postings across experience levels to identify which candidates are most vulnerable.' captured-sheet='Fraud Rate by Required Experience' id='3' />
                  <story-point caption='Compare the overall proportion of genuine and fraudulent job postings to evaluate recruitment platform reliability' captured-sheet='Genuine vs Fraudulent Split' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='Evaluate the percentage of fraudulent postings within each industry to identify the industries with the highest fraud risk.' captured-sheet='Fraud Rate by Industry' id='5' />
                  <story-point caption='Analyze the relationship between required experience and employment type to understand recruitment patterns and identify potential fraud targets.' captured-sheet='Required Experience vs Employment Type' id='6' />
                  <story-point caption='Visualize the geographic distribution of fraudulent job postings to identify locations with higher recruitment fraud activity' captured-sheet='Fraud Map by Location' id='7' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='23444' hidden='true' id='6' story-point-id='1' type-v2='text' w='64862' x='26575' y='47718'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This chart highlights the distribution of fraudulent job postings across different industries. It helps identify which industries experience the highest number of fake job advertisements. A higher fraud count indicates that scammers are actively targeting job seekers within those sectors because they receive a large number of applications.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='27905' hidden='true' id='7' story-point-id='2' type-v2='text' w='83957' x='3839' y='41909'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Different employment types attract different levels of fraud. This visualization compares full-time, part-time, contract, internship, and temporary jobs to determine where fraudulent recruiters are most active. Flexible work opportunities often receive more applications, making them attractive targets for scammers.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='26971' hidden='true' id='8' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='94587' x='984' y='46888'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This chart analyzes fraud rates based on the required experience level. It reveals whether scammers primarily target fresh graduates, entry-level professionals, or experienced candidates. Understanding this pattern helps recruitment platforms design better protection mechanisms for vulnerable applicants.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='13797' hidden='true' id='9' story-point-id='4' type-v2='text' w='90157' x='4232' y='39004'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This visualization provides a high-level overview of the dataset by comparing genuine and fraudulent job postings. It immediately communicates the overall level of recruitment fraud and serves as the starting point for deeper investigation.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='15145' hidden='true' id='10' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='85827' x='98' y='25415'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Unlike fraud count, this chart measures fraud as a percentage of all postings within each industry. This allows fair comparison between industries of different sizes and identifies sectors where fraud represents the greatest risk.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='23444' hidden='true' id='11' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='81594' x='8858' y='42635'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This chart compares employment types with required experience levels to understand which combinations are most common. It helps identify whether fraudulent postings tend to target entry-level full-time positions, internships, or contract opportunities.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='15456' id='12' story-point-id='7' type-v2='text' w='73524' x='8465' y='64212'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This geographic visualization identifies where fraudulent job postings are concentrated. It enables organizations to compare recruitment fraud across locations and prioritize monitoring efforts in regions with higher fraud activity.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{ED602F29-5F5F-4824-8F77-0F10090355C7}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
